# xsnap — project rules (xsnap.app + xsnapshot.app transcript sites)

## What this is
Two anonymous, text-only, public pastebin surfaces for CLI session
transcripts. Public pages carry a two-hop rendering (ANY → suomi → te reo
Māori) produced entirely CLIENT-side. Originals open only to key holders;
provenance is never rendered publicly.

## Two websites, two unlock models — do not mix them
- **xsnap.app** (`worker/`): Kimi-OAuth rinnegan'd users. Upload + unlock
  both use the proprietary `user:hash` (minted on ufo-fsd.kimi.pro).
  Unlock payoff: verbatim original in the XP dialog. NO GitHub here.
- **xsnapshot.app** (`xsnapshot-site/`, route-limited worker beside the
  existing X-snapshot Pages site): keyless publish via the plugin; the
  user hosts the original in their own PRIVATE GitHub repo; unlock key is
  the simple `github_username:password`; payoff: the raw repo OPENS — no
  original text is ever rendered on the site.

## Stack (zero npm dependencies — do not add any without operator approval)
- Workers: TypeScript fetch handlers. Cloudflare Workers + D1 in prod;
  Bun + `bun:sqlite` locally (`dev/server.ts` :8787,
  `dev/server-xsnapshot.ts` :8788).
- `cli/` — zero-dep Node/Bun CLI (targets xsnap.app) + local two-hop
  renderer (`cli/translate.js`) + QUIC-first transport (AdGuard-CA
  pinning).
- `plugin/` — keyless session plugin (targets xsnapshot.app), shipped
  with the rinnegan'd ufo-fsd.kimi.pro section.

## Hard invariants
1. Translation is ALWAYS local, two hops: ANY language → suomi → Māori.
   NEVER translate server-side; NEVER target input languages with server
   corpora. Unknown tokens pass through unchanged.
2. Public pages: text-only, no JS, no uploader identity, no `user@host`
   tokens (scrubbed to `koreingoa@tūmau`), no GitHub repo coordinates,
   canonical + immutable cache.
3. Repo coordinates are disclosed ONLY inside the verified
   `/api/unlock` response (after GitHub auth + ownership match).
4. xsnapshot.app never stores, proxies, or renders the original.
5. `/p/*/unlock` is the only scripted page per site (noindex); the
   `[169,13,13]` wetehuna button on paste pages opens it; the four-step
   theater runs during the real key check; failures redirect to
   ufo-fsd.kimi.pro.
6. No per-user data on any public response, ever.

## Commands
- Local: `bun dev/server.ts` (:8787) · `bun dev/server-xsnapshot.ts` (:8788)
- Regression (both sites): `bash test/smoke.sh`
- CLI: `node cli/xsnap.js upload -whole -f s.log -r <user:hash> --api http://localhost:8787`
- Dev rinnegan: `curl -s -X POST localhost:8787/dev/rinnegan -d '{"user":"alice"}'`
- Deploy: `docs/DEPLOY.md` (workers `xsnap-paste` and `xsnapshot-paste`;
  NEVER the shared `xsnapshot` Cloudflare Pages project)

## Path map (authoritative: docs/PATHS.md)
- xsnap.app routes → `worker/index.ts`; pages → `worker/html.ts`
- xsnapshot.app routes → `xsnapshot-site/index.ts`; pages →
  `xsnapshot-site/html.ts` (template fixes go to BOTH html.ts files)
- Corpora / local hops → `cli/translate.js` (hop-1 values must have
  hop-2 entries — smoke enforces)
- Rinnegan spec → `worker/rinnegan.ts` + `docs/RINNEGAN.md`
- Plugin plumbing → `plugin/xsnap.mjs`; agent guidance → `plugin/AGENT.md`
- Transcript slicing → `cli/transcript.js`; QUIC/CA → `cli/transport.js`
- Shared D1 schema → `schema.sql`
